WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:23.910
Judge Man cheated at gambling and gave me trouble.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:28.070
But my drawing skills are second to none!

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:32.420
In the end, Lady Luck smiled upon me.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.560
But I can't waste time.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:41.000
The remaining members of The Big Five could be targeting Shizuka.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.500
Hang on, Shizuka!

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:51.560
A Man's Path  Honda's Honorable Defeat

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:00.200
This area looks safe.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.950
Actually, there may be traps.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.340
Stay alert.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.200
Otogi!

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.310
It's true!

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:13.970
Stop saying things that can scare Shizuka!

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:18.880
I'm glad I was able to reunite with you two.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.750
Right?  You'll be fine because we'll protect you.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.220
How can you promise that?

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.170
Knock it off!

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.220
You're all talk, Honda!

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.200
What!

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.000
Please stop!  Both of you!

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.400
Instead, how's my brother doing?

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.800
Well...

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.570
He's probably dueling.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.840
If you defeat us, we'll release you from this virtual world.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:55.220
But if you refuse to duel, we won't let you leave this world.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:56.950
The Big Five.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:05.050
Since there's five of them, even non-duelists like us will have to duel.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:05.900
Otogi!

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.800
But since Honda is with us, we'll be fine.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:12.470
Why?

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.060
Because Honda is my brother's dueling teacher.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.460
Honda, I thought you've never dueled-

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:28.350
If anyone challenges us to a duel, I'll pummel 'em all!

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:39.620
Since we we each defeated a member of The Big Five, there are two left.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:45.370
I'm not worried about Kaiba, but what if they attack someone else?

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.350
Dammit!

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:47.800
Jonouchi!

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:48.880
Wait!

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.310
What's this?

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:55.480
What?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.130
What is this?

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.000
It's a door, right?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.990
Looks that way, but...

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.520
It's suspicious.  We should be careful.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:08.050
It must be the way out.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:10.580
Shizuka!  No!

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.140
Are we back at the hanger?

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:29.150
No.  I don't see the Battle Ship.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.580
We must be in a different one.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:36.020
At least we escaped that weird virtual world.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.350
Yeah.  Maybe the others are back too.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:40.500
Thank goodness.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.910
I was waiting for you.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.060
We haven't escaped.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.080
What a weak roster.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:52.170
I'm Soichiro Ota, one of The Big Five.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.170
Why are you dressed like that?

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.900
This is my Deck Master, Robotic Knight.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.620
Before that annoying Seto Kaiba was President...

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:10.390
...I was in charge of Kaiba Corporation's military factories.

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.320
I was known as "The Factory's Devil Sergeant."

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.100
Let's begin the duel.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:22.500
My opponent will be the first person who entered this room.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.080
You.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:25.700
Me?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.230
What should I do, Honda?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.000
Wait!  I'll be your opponent!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.880
It's not fair to duel an amateur!

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.550
No!  I'll duel!

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.020
You haven't dueled much either.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.140
This isn't the time to show off to Shizuka.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.490
If I don't duel now, when will I?

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.060
Protecting each other is pointless.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:51.560
Because none of you can defeat me!

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:54.570
Damn.  He's very confident.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.660
The pain we feel in this world is the same as in the real world.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:03.780
Therefore, damage during a duel will be real too.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:08.010
I can't let Shizuka duel, no matter what!

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.950
I won't let Shizuka duel.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.830
Then how about this?

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:15.390
What?

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.540
The two of us will duel you.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:21.640
If you win, you'll get two bodies at once.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:25.500
Let's have a more efficient and interesting duel.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.200
How about 3-on-1?

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.150
What?

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:33.400
One of me, three of you.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.940
But I'll take the bodies of anyone who loses.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.770
The two of us is enough!

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.240
I have my reasons.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.750
I'll take all three of your bodies.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:47.940
So Yugi and the others...

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.150
...must've won!

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:54.200
You three are pathetic, but you'll have a better chance if you work together.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.030
Be grateful.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.050
You got a big mouth!

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.400
I bet you don't know!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.070
That Honda taught my brother how to duel!

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.200
Shizuka!

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:08.610
Honda, Otogi, I'll do my best!

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.560
Do your best?

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.040
No, Shizuka!  You can't duel!

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:16.480
Wear a Duel Disk.

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:23.400
Wow!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.950
Shizuka, you really shouldn't duel.

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:32.070
I'll be fine because you're by my side.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.120
Shizuka...

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.260
This is bad.

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:37.950
Build your decks.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:40.370
Touch the cards you need.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:43.280
Umm...  Honda?

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.040
Choose 40 cards.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:51.580
Instead of only picking strong monster cards, choose a variety of spells and traps too.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:52.200
Okay.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.650
Umm, how's this...  And this...

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.590
This is a female warrior.

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:01.260
This card is...

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:07.200
When you're done, choose a Deck Master from your deck.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:11.260
My Deck Master is Strike Ninja.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.200
Mine is...  Umm...

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.880
Miss Goddess with the Third Eye.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.440
You don't need to say "Miss."

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.820
I choose Super Roboyarou!

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:25.850
You seem ready.

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.490
Shall we begin?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.100
What?

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:40.100
Since it's 3-on-1, the rules are different.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:46.100
You can work together to attack me, but you're not allowed to discuss with each other.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:50.100
After you three act, then it's my turn.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.000
"Ladies first" is fine.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.700
Honda, I put my deck into this Duel Disk, right?

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.220
That's right, Shizuka.

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:06.850
Start the duel!

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.190
Do your best, Shizuka!

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.640
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.570
What should I do...

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.260
This!  Shadow Tamer!

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.000
My brother would attack!

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:22.670
I summon Shadow Tamer in attack position!

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.920
Attack position?

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.540
Did I do something wrong?

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:32.150
She'll be an easy target.

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.720
Honda.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.420
It's fine... right?

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.650
Of course it's fine!  I'll fix it.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.290
It's not fine at all.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.770
I end my turn.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.170
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.400
I can't let him attack Shizuka.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.030
I summon Cyber Commander in attack position!

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.600
Attack me instead.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.710
I end my turn!

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:10.980
Honda summoned it in attack position so that Shizuka won't be the target.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.060
My turn!

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:13.660
I draw!

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:15.690
C'mon, Otogi.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:18.810
Summon a weak monster in attack position.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:23.230
Then it'll be a 1-in-3 chance that Shizuka will be attacked.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.340
Come out, The 13th Grave!

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.980
In defense position!

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:30.770
Otogi!  How dare you!

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.420
Are you giving up on Shizuka?

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:34.950
I end my turn!

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.380
Fine.  It's my turn.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:38.570
I draw.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.400
I summon Giga-Tech Wolf.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.190
Attack Shadow Tamer!

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:48.360
That punk is attacking Shizuka!

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.700
Take damage equal to the attack point difference!

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.070
Shizuka!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.940
I heard Shizuka scream!

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:05.470
Yeah.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:07.860
Is it The Big Five?

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:08.980
Shizuka...

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:10.680
Shizuka...

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.730
Shizuka!

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:31.960
Shizuka!

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.420
Shizuka!

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.420
Don't move!

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.400
What?

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:41.400
You can't leave your field during the duel.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.680
Say what?

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.110
I'm fine.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.280
Shizuka...

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:52.290
In this duel, damage inflicts real pain.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.600
Shizuka can't take any more damage.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:59.260
My turn isn't over yet!

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:00.440
What?

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:04.200
I activate my Deck Master's ability, Supporting Bombardment!

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:08.200
For every Machine-Type Monster I discard...

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.470
...you take 500 points of damage!

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:21.420
Shizuka!

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:26.720
I set a card and end my turn.

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.150
Are you okay, Shizuka?

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:30.300
Yes!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:31.980
It's my turn!

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.630
This one has the most defense points.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.660
Good.  Focus on defense, Shizuka!

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:45.740
Right!  I summon The Forgiving Maiden!

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.180
Attack position again?

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:53.850
She doesn't know how to set a card on her Duel Disk!

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:58.700
Shizuka, you have to set the card horizontally instead of vertically for defense position.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:12:59.560
What?

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.100
You're not allowed to discuss.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:04.790
Let her do it over!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:09.960
You can't change its position until your next turn.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.630
I end my turn.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.240
This is bad.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.600
If he uses Supporting Bombardment again...

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.640
I have to do something.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.240
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:24.680
Block Attack.  Good.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.420
I'll use this spell card to switch Shizuka's monster to defense position.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:32.220
I activate Block Attack from my hand!

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.660
I won't let you!

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:35.960
I flip over my trap card!

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:39.640
Riryoku Field, destroy Block Attack!

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:46.360
Damn!  I couldn't do anything!

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:47.730
I end my turn!

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:54.710
Big brother!  Look!

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:02.760
That's Kaiba Corporation's military factory that I destroyed.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:08.830
Ota, prove your loyalty to me.

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.490
Destroy Alcatraz's factory.

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.700
S-Say what?

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.530
The factory?

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:20.220
I put my heart into building my factory!

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:22.900
And you want me to destroy it?

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:26.090
Actually, it's my factory.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:36.130
Why is Noa obsessed with me?

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:43.500
He's so rude that I'm now more curious than angry.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:48.570
Get to the point and show yourself!

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:56.160
Making demands on a ruler proves that I'm superior to everyone.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:15:02.010
Seto, I'm proving that by playing with your emotions.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.550
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.980
If I can get him to play my game...

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:11.440
Otogi, forget about counterattacking.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.150
Play a card that protects Shizuka.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.560
Yaranzo in defense position!

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.540
Otogi!  I misjudged you!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.630
That won't protect Shizuka!

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:25.060
I set a card and end my turn.

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:26.450
My turn.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:30.480
I tribute Giga-Tech Wolf to summon Machine King!

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:39.250
For every faceup Machine-Type monster on the field, Machine King gains 100 attack points.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:47.200
Cyber Commander and Machine King are Machine-Type, so it gains 200 attack points.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:48.800
Time to battle!

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:52.060
Machine King, destroy The Forgiving Maiden!

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.960
Go, Cyber Commander!

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:59.320
Honda!  Wait!  Let me handle it!

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.970
I'll protect Shizuka!

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.010
Honda!

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:12.830
With my defending monster, we wouldn't have taken damage!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.350
Really?  Say that earlier!

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:18.410
It's common sense!

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:22.050
Next, I activate Card of Sanctity from my hand.

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:26.980
All players must draw until they have six cards in their hands.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:32.600
Now that I've resupplied, I'll resume my attack.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.700
He still...

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:35.030
...can attack?

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:39.970
Due to my Deck Master's ability, I discard three Machine-Type monsters.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.900
Supporting Bombardment!

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:57.060
I set one card and end my turn.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:59.210
My turn.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.120
I draw.

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:02.500
Umm...

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.320
I summon Lady Panther in defense position.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:11.760
And I switch The Forgiving Maiden to defense position and end my turn.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:14.200
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:18.480
I summon Command Angel in defense position!

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:23.920
My turn!  I summon Dark Assailant in defense position!

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.000
What's wrong?  Ending your turn already?

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:36.100
With so many defending monsters, your attack won't reach us.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:40.600
And you've used your Deck Master's ability so much that you're running out of cards!

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.240
You can't do Supporting Bombardment anymore!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:47.040
Otogi, you thought of everything.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:54.000
And since we have a lot of monsters, we can tribute them to summon high-Level monsters.

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.570
Not good enough.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:57.930
You forgot about my trap card.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:58.600
What?

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:03.060
I activate my trap card!  Backup Soldier!

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.990
Backup Soldier?

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:08.420
Since I have at least five monster cards in my graveyard...

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:14.870
...I can return up to three monsters with 1500-or-fewer attack points to my hand.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:20.150
Giga-Tech Wolf, Cyber Falcon and Ground Attacker Bugroth resurrect.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:28.200
I discard the three cards that I just resurrected.

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:31.680
I activate my Deck Master's ability!  Supporting Bombardment!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.120
You only resurrected them to replenish your bullets?

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:36.990
Supporting Bombardment!

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.260
I end my turn.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:46.900
My turn.

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:51.870
I was waiting for this moment.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:56.240
I activate the Continuous Spell Clockwork Night from my hand!

00:18:56.480 --> 00:19:00.730
All monsters on the field become Machine-Type!

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:01.730
What?

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:03.460
All become Machines?

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:12.340
My monster gains attack points, but your monsters lose 500 attack points.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:19.930
Machine King gains 100 attack points for every Machine-Type monster on the field.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:24.970
And Clockwork Night raises its attack points by 500!

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:27.270
3400?

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:28.640
It's fine.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:32.600
Even though it's powerful, it can only attack once.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:35.710
As long as we're in defense position, we won't take big damage.

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:38.100
Are you sure?

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:40.980
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Short Circuit!

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.330
Hey!

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:51.010
It forces them into attack position!

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:55.670
This effect forces your monsters to switch to attack position.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:20:02.540
And they can't switch positions, attack, or use their effects for one turn.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:04.550
For real?

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.310
If he attacks, we're helpless!

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:10.620
Your monsters have short circuited and can't move!

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:14.620
Machine King, attack The Forgiving Maiden!

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:18.970
You can't protect her from this attack!

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:21.330
Damn!  What can we do?

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:24.160
If we only had a monster unaffected by Short Circuit...

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:26.430
There is one!

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:27.600
Fire!

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:30.670
Go!  Super Roboyarou!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.480
Wait, Honda!

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.510
If you lose your Deck Master, you'll be...

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:37.900
I use my Deck Master's ability to set a card!

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:40.610
And Super Roboyarou gains attack points!

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:43.780
You can't avoid this attack with that effect!

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:51.790
Honda!

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:55.390
This was the best move I could do.

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:57.830
I'm sorry, Shizuka.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:02.770
I lied about teaching Jonouchi how to duel.

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:06.220
As you can see, I'm an amateur.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:09.440
Otogi, take care of Shizuka!

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:13.110
Since you lost your Deck Master, it's game over.

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:15.710
Honda!

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:20.820
Honda!

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.190
Honda...

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.280
One down.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:28.990
I end my turn.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:47.960
No way!  The Big Five defeated Honda?

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:50.830
Due to the shock, Shizuka can only cry.

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:53.900
But this duel can't be stopped!

00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:56.950
Otogi and Shizuka will both be defeated!

00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:58.920
Stand up, Shizuka!

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:03.000
Don't let Honda's sacrifice go to waste!  Fight back!

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:07.340
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
St. Joan
The Trinity's Attack

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:08.860
Duel, standby!

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:20.650
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:29.600
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:34.570
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:34.570 --> 00:22:38.540
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:38.970 --> 00:22:46.510
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.080
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:54.850
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:54.850 --> 00:23:04.960
And walk it without stopping

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:12.570
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:21.540
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:29.520
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:39.360
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
